        "name": "skill",
        "path": "andurel skill",
        "short": "Show or install the embedded Andurel skill",
        "category": "skill",
        "meta": {
          "group": "skill",
          "summary": "Show or install the embedded Andurel skill",
          "when_to_use": [
            "Arm a coding agent with Andurel layer and CLI rules."
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel skill show",
            "andurel skill install --harness pi"
          ],
          "mutating": false,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": false,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "sync",
        "path": "andurel sync",
        "short": "Refresh derived files from a source of truth",
        "category": "sync",
        "meta": {
          "group": "sync",
          "summary": "Refresh derived files from a source of truth",
          "when_to_use": [
            "Regenerate *_templ.go, narsilc output, or Inertia routes/payloads and emails."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Creating application-owned files is andurel generate.",
            "Downloading binaries is andurel tool sync."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel sync --help",
            "andurel sync queries",
            "andurel sync routes --json"
          ],
          "mutating": false,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": false,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false,
          "skip_dry_run_check": true
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "tool",
        "path": "andurel tool",
        "aliases": [
          "tools",
          "t"
        ],
        "short": "Manage project tools and binaries",
        "category": "tool",
        "meta": {
          "group": "tool",
          "summary": "Manage project tools and binaries",
          "when_to_use": [
            "List, pin, download, or launch lockfile tools.",
            "Tool versions are pinned in andurel.toml; andurel.lock holds the per-platform SHA-256 digests."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Application code generation is under generate, not tool."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root",
            "andurel.toml",
            "andurel.lock"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel tool --help",
            "andurel tool list --json",
            "andurel tool sync"
          ],
          "mutating": false,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": true,
          "supports_ids_only": true,
          "supports_count": true
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "upgrade",
        "path": "andurel upgrade",
        "aliases": [
          "up"
        ],
        "short": "Upgrade the project to this CLI version",
        "category": "upgrade",
        "meta": {
          "group": "upgrade",
          "summary": "Upgrade the project to this CLI version",
          "when_to_use": [
            "After installing a newer Andurel CLI: re-pin pkg modules, sync tools, and list the manual actions to apply."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Commit first. Use packages update to bump pkg modules without a framework upgrade."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root"
          ],
          "next": [
            "andurel inspect upgrade-notes --from \u003cprevious-version\u003e"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel upgrade --dry-run --json",
            "andurel upgrade"
          ],
          "mutating": true,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": true,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": true,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "verify",
        "path": "andurel verify",
        "short": "Check formatting, vet, layer boundaries, frontend, and generated code",
        "category": "verify",
        "meta": {
          "group": "verify",
          "summary": "Check formatting, vet, layer boundaries, frontend, and generated code",
          "args": "[packages...]",
          "when_to_use": [
            "After a change, before commit: gofmt, go fix, go vet, the typed persistence and transaction boundary checks, the package.json typecheck script, and generated-code drift.",
            "Pass Go package patterns to scope gofmt, go fix, go vet, and layers to those packages; generated drift and the frontend typecheck stay whole-project.",
            "A missing generation binary fails the generated step; apply the rule's fix, or pass --skip-generated to mark the step skipped. Rules lists every rule and its fix.",
            "Without node_modules the frontend step fails with an install hint; pass --no-frontend to skip it explicitly.",
            "Read each violation's fix field and apply it; a failed run exits 9 (verification_failed).",
            "With --with-tests, check the go test step's skipped_packages: packages listed there ran no tests (DB tests skip without Docker) even though the step is ok.",
            "With --with-tests, tests that called t.Skip are listed in the go test step's skipped_tests as {package, test, reason}; they do not fail the run either.",
            "Unresolved inertia.FromStruct payload roots are listed in the generated step's warnings and do not fail verify; andurel sync payloads --strict turns them into errors."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "verify is read-only; fix the reported issues yourself and re-run."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel verify",
            "andurel verify --json",
            "andurel verify ./internal/docs/...",
            "andurel verify --with-tests",
            "andurel verify --skip-generated",
            "andurel verify --no-frontend"
          ],
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "gofmt",
              "summary": "every Go file is gofmt-clean",
              "fix": "gofmt -w \u003cfile\u003e",
              "layer": "format"
            },
            {
              "id": "go fix",
              "summary": "go fix reports no automatic rewrites",
              "fix": "go fix ./...",
              "layer": "build"
            },
            {
              "id": "queries-import",
              "summary": "only domains/** imports domains/internal/queries",
              "fix": "call a method on a domains receiver instead of generated queries",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "db-handle",
              "summary": "outside domains no SQL methods or SQL drivers; Connection/Transaction are persistence wiring",
              "fix": "move the database access into a domains method and call it on a receiver",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "tx-unwrap",
              "summary": "storage.Unwrap is referenced only under domains/**",
              "fix": "bind a domain receiver with receiver.InTx(tx) instead of unwrapping the transaction",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "tx-escape",
              "summary": "a storage.AtomicOps callback uses only dependencies bound inside the transaction",
              "fix": "bind the dependency at the top of the callback (dep := value.InTx(tx)) and use the bound value",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "tx-public-call",
              "summary": "a storage.AtomicOps callback does not call an exported method on its own receiver",
              "fix": "move the shared logic into an unexported helper that takes bound dependencies as parameters",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "tx-layer",
              "summary": "storage.AtomicOps and storage.Transactor are used only in services, domains, and internal/runtime",
              "fix": "move transaction orchestration into a service; run 'andurel patterns show service'",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "domain-transport",
              "summary": "domains/** imports no HTTP, Inertia, routing, handler, middleware, or route package",
              "fix": "keep domains free of transport packages; move the adapter to handlers or services",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "entity-columns",
              "summary": "every automatic generated query column maps to an exported andurel tag on its domain entity",
              "fix": "add an exported field tagged andurel:\"\u003ccolumn\u003e\", or narrow the query columns and run 'andurel sync queries'",
              "layer": "layers"
            },
            {
              "id": "setup",
              "summary": "project setup is complete: managed tool binaries and frontend dependencies are installed",
              "fix": "run the setup commands named by each violation ('andurel tool sync', '\u003cpackage manager\u003e install')",
              "layer": "setup"
            },
            {
              "id": "frontend",
              "summary": "the package.json typecheck script passes when the scaffold defines one",
              "fix": "fix the reported TypeScript errors and re-run the project package manager's typecheck script",
              "layer": "frontend"
            },
            {
              "id": "frontend-route-usage",
              "summary": "frontend modules do not call full-URL route helpers at module initialization; use .path() or call while rendering",
              "fix": "move the call into the component render, an event handler, or a function called after configureRouteHosts; use routes.\u003cname\u003e.path(...) for a relative URL",
              "layer": "frontend"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-config",
              "summary": "andurel.content.toml parses, declares a supported schemaVersion, and its include/exclude globs are valid",
              "fix": "fix the reported andurel.content.toml entry; see 'andurel verify --help' for the schema",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-catalog",
              "summary": "every declared content catalog entry resolves to an included Markdown file",
              "fix": "add the missing Markdown file or correct the catalog entry's file path",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-slug",
              "summary": "content catalog slugs are non-empty, match the declared pattern, and are unique",
              "fix": "give each catalog entry a unique slug that matches the [slugs].pattern",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-required",
              "summary": "every path listed in andurel.content.toml required exists",
              "fix": "create the required file or directory, or remove it from the required list",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-link",
              "summary": "local Markdown links and images resolve inside the project; configured anchors exist",
              "fix": "correct the link target, add the missing file, or fix the anchor; external and site-absolute URLs are not fetched",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "content-checker",
              "summary": "each declared content checker exits 0 within its timeout from its declared working directory",
              "fix": "fix the checker's reported diagnostics or its run/dir/timeoutSeconds entry in andurel.content.toml",
              "layer": "content"
            },
            {
              "id": "generated",
              "summary": "generated templ, email, queries, routes, and payload output is up to date",
              "fix": "run the owning andurel sync command",
              "layer": "generated"
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-tool",
              "summary": "a required generation binary is installed; run 'andurel tool sync'",
              "fix": "andurel tool sync",
              "layer": "generated"
            }
          ],
          "mutating": false,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": true,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "agent_notes": "Discover commands, then run a specific subcommand.",
    "category": "root",
    "meta": {
      "summary": "Andurel CLI for humans and agents",
      "when_to_use": [
        "Discover commands, then run a specific subcommand."
      ],
      "when_not_to_use": [
        "Do not guess generator names; run andurel commands --json first."
      ],
      "examples": [
        "andurel commands --json",
        "andurel --help",
        "andurel new myapp"
      ],
      "mutating": false,
      "supports_dry_run": false,
      "supports_json": true,
      "supports_jq": false,
      "supports_ids_only": false,
      "supports_count": false
    },
    "commands": [
      {
        "name": "build",
        "path": "andurel build",
        "short": "Build every application process for production",
        "long": "Build every cmd/* process that has a main package, except cmd/seeds, and\ncompile all assets for production deployment.\n\nThis command:\n  • Generates Go from .templ files (email + Inertia root)\n  • Generates narsilc code when domains/**/*.sql contains SQL files\n  • Compiles Tailwind utilities in email templates\n  • Builds Vite client assets and the SSR bundle (when Inertia is configured)\n  • Builds cmd/app, cmd/queue, cmd/migrate, and cmd/ssr into dist/ (or --output-dir)\n  • Injects the version string via ldflags (from --version or git describe)\n\nClient assets and the SSR bundle are embedded in the binaries: assets/assets.go\nembeds assets/dist, including assets/dist/ssr/ssr.js, so the app and SSR\nprocesses need no asset files beside the binary at runtime.\n\nUse --only to build a subset, and --json for an artifact manifest.\n\nUse --output-dir to isolate every writable build intermediate. The project\nsource tree, including assets/dist and generated Go files, is left untouched:\nandurel copies the project into a private staging directory, runs templ,\nnarsilc, email, Vite and Go builds there, and publishes only the finished\nbinaries. Relative --output-dir paths resolve from the project root. The\nmanifest reports absolute artifact paths and isolated=true. Two builds of the\nsame project with different output directories do not share writable paths.\n\nIsolated builds copy an existing node_modules snapshot instead of running the\npackage manager against the shared source tree; run your package manager\ninstall command first when dependencies change. Dependencies are copied as\nregular files, never hardlinked, so a build plugin cannot mutate the source\ninode. Symlinks whose targets resolve inside the project or the dependency\nsnapshot are rewritten to their staged counterparts; a symlink that resolves\noutside both is rejected rather than followed, because writes through it could\nnot be kept private to the build stage. Staging directories are removed on\nnormal success and failure.\n\nBinary publication is all-or-nothing across every selected process. A\npublication journal is written before the first rename; a build interrupted\nbetween renames is rolled back to the previous complete artifact set by the\nnext build. A committed set is kept as a unit, so a new app is never paired\nwith a previous SSR binary. A SIGKILL can leave an unreferenced staging\ndirectory behind, but it is never used by a later build.\n\nWithout --output-dir the historical in-place layout is preserved: binaries in\ndist/, Vite output in assets/dist/, tools in bin/. Use that mode when the\ndevelopment asset tree should be refreshed by the build.\n\nEvery process loads .env at startup. Runtime configuration by process:\n  • app: database, HTTP/hosts, sessions, cookies, auth, email, cache, queue,\n    Inertia, and telemetry configuration\n  • queue: database, queue, cache, email, and telemetry configuration\n  • migrate: database configuration only\n  • ssr: INERTIA_* configuration only, plus a JavaScript runtime on PATH\n\nSee andurel patterns show deploy for the start order (migrate → ssr → app +\nqueue), shared environment, and health checks.",
        "usage": "andurel build [flags]",
        "examples": "andurel build\n  andurel build --version 1.2.3\n  andurel build --only app,queue\n  andurel build --output-dir /tmp/app-build\n  andurel build --json",
        "local_flags": [
          {
            "name": "only",
            "usage": "Build only the named processes (comma-separated, e.g. app,queue)",
            "default": "[]",
            "type": "stringSlice"
          },
          {
            "name": "output-dir",
            "usage": "Publish binaries into an isolated output directory (relative paths resolve from the project root)",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "version",
            "usage": "Set the application version (injected via ldflags)",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "inherited_flags": [
          {
            "name": "agent",
            "usage": "Emit structured output optimized for agents",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "count",
            "usage": "Emit one raw resource count when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "ids-only",
            "usage": "Emit one resource identifier per line when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "jq",
            "usage": "Select a field path (for example .routes[0].name) from command data and emit JSON directly",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "json",
            "usage": "Emit JSON output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "md",
            "usage": "Emit Markdown output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "quiet",
            "usage": "Suppress non-essential human output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "verbose",
            "usage": "Emit verbose output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ],
        "agent_notes": "Compile every cmd/* process with a main package (except seeds) and the client assets into dist/. Client assets and assets/dist/ssr/ssr.js are embedded in the binaries; no asset files are needed beside them at runtime. Use --only to build a subset, and --json for an artifact manifest with path, size, and version. Runtime environment: app needs the full config; queue needs database, queue, email, cache, and telemetry; migrate needs DB_*; ssr needs INERTIA_* and a JavaScript runtime.",
        "category": "build",
        "meta": {
          "group": "build",
          "summary": "Build every application process for production",
          "when_to_use": [
            "Compile every cmd/* process with a main package (except seeds) and the client assets into dist/.",
            "Client assets and assets/dist/ssr/ssr.js are embedded in the binaries; no asset files are needed beside them at runtime.",
            "Use --only to build a subset, and --json for an artifact manifest with path, size, and version.",
            "Runtime environment: app needs the full config; queue needs database, queue, email, cache, and telemetry; migrate needs DB_*; ssr needs INERTIA_* and a JavaScript runtime."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Use andurel run for local development.",
            "Read andurel patterns show deploy for the migrate → ssr → app + queue start order and health checks."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root",
            "cmd/\u003cprocess\u003e/main.go for every process to build"
          ],
          "next": [
            "andurel patterns show deploy"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel build",
            "andurel build --version 1.2.3",
            "andurel build --only app,queue",
            "andurel build --json"
          ],
          "mutating": true,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": false,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false,
          "skip_dry_run_check": true
        }
      },
