      {
        "name": "doctor",
        "path": "andurel doctor",
        "aliases": [
          "doc"
        ],
        "short": "Run diagnostic checks on the project",
        "long": "Run comprehensive diagnostic checks to verify your Andurel project health.\n\nThis command will check:\n  • Environment (Go version, latest stable Andurel release)\n  • Configuration (andurel.lock, first-run setup, runtime configuration and database connectivity, Inertia SSR readiness)\n  • Code quality (go vet, go mod tidy)\n  • Code generation (templ, email renderers, narsilc, and Inertia route helpers and payload types when configured)\n\nRuntime configuration and the database probe run the project's own read-only\ncheck (internal/configcheck), so the check cannot drift from the config\nconstructor cmd/app uses. Missing or malformed required values and an\nunreachable database fail; a check that cannot run is reported as skipped,\nnever as a pass.",
        "usage": "andurel doctor [flags]",
        "examples": "andurel doctor\n  andurel doctor --verbose",
        "local_flags": [
          {
            "name": "verbose",
            "usage": "Emit verbose diagnostic output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ],
        "inherited_flags": [
          {
            "name": "agent",
            "usage": "Emit structured output optimized for agents",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "count",
            "usage": "Emit one raw resource count when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "ids-only",
            "usage": "Emit one resource identifier per line when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "jq",
            "usage": "Select a field path (for example .routes[0].name) from command data and emit JSON directly",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "json",
            "usage": "Emit JSON output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "md",
            "usage": "Emit Markdown output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "quiet",
            "usage": "Suppress non-essential human output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ],
        "agent_notes": "Verify health and generated-file drift after changes. Check first-run setup, runtime configuration and bounded database connectivity through the generated internal/configcheck helper, and Inertia SSR readiness. Read json/agent output for each check's status: a skipped check is blocked on a prerequisite and is never reported as a pass.",
        "category": "doctor",
        "meta": {
          "group": "doctor",
          "summary": "Run diagnostic checks on the project",
          "when_to_use": [
            "Verify health and generated-file drift after changes.",
            "Check first-run setup, runtime configuration and bounded database connectivity through the generated internal/configcheck helper, and Inertia SSR readiness.",
            "Read json/agent output for each check's status: a skipped check is blocked on a prerequisite and is never reported as a pass."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Doctor is read-only; it does not write generated files."
          ],
          "prerequisites": [
            "Andurel project root"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel doctor --json",
            "andurel doctor --verbose"
          ],
          "mutating": false,
          "requires_project": true,
          "supports_dry_run": false,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": true,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false
        }
