      {
        "name": "new",
        "path": "andurel new",
        "aliases": [
          "n"
        ],
        "short": "Stand up a new Andurel project",
        "long": "Stand up a complete Andurel project with the given name.\n\nGenerates the full project structure including handlers, domains, services,\nroutes, middleware, database migrations, and configuration files. Creation is\noffline: it installs no dependencies and needs no database. The printed next\nsteps and the generated README share one Quick Start:\n\n  1. cd \u003cproject\u003e \u0026\u0026 andurel tool sync \u0026\u0026 \u003cpackage manager\u003e install\n  2. cp .env.example .env, set the required values, create the database if\n     needed, then andurel db migrate up\n  3. andurel doctor, andurel run, andurel verify\n\nProjects use Inertia React with pnpm by default. Pass --ui to choose another\nInertia combination (react|vue|svelte / pnpm|bun|npm). Persistence uses\nnarsilc-generated queries; it stays inactive until an annotated query is\nadded to a domain, for example domains/user.sql.\n\nPass --harness to install the bundled Andurel skill for your agent harness\nduring creation (comma-separated or repeated, as in andurel skill install).\nWith no --harness the skill is not installed; the next steps print an explicit\ninstallation example.",
        "usage": "andurel new [project-name] [flags]",
        "local_flags": [
          {
            "name": "diff",
            "usage": "Include a text diff preview in structured output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "dry-run",
            "usage": "Preview project files without creating them",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "harness",
            "usage": "Install the Andurel skill for these harnesses: codex, claude, pi, opencode, crush (comma-separated or repeated)",
            "default": "[]",
            "type": "stringSlice"
          },
          {
            "name": "ui",
            "usage": "UI combination: react|vue|svelte / pnpm|bun|npm (default: react/pnpm)",
            "default": "react/pnpm",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "inherited_flags": [
          {
            "name": "agent",
            "usage": "Emit structured output optimized for agents",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "count",
            "usage": "Emit one raw resource count when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "ids-only",
            "usage": "Emit one resource identifier per line when supported",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "jq",
            "usage": "Select a field path (for example .routes[0].name) from command data and emit JSON directly",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "json",
            "usage": "Emit JSON output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "md",
            "usage": "Emit Markdown output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "quiet",
            "usage": "Suppress non-essential human output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          },
          {
            "name": "verbose",
            "usage": "Emit verbose output",
            "default": "false",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ],
        "agent_notes": "Create a new application directory from the current scaffold. Creation is offline: it installs no dependencies and needs no database.",
        "category": "new",
        "meta": {
          "group": "new",
          "summary": "Stand up a new Andurel project",
          "args": "[project-name]",
          "details": [
            "Quick Start, also printed by andurel new and in the generated README: andurel tool sync; pnpm install (or bun/npm to match --ui); cp .env.example .env and set the required values; andurel db create (only if the database does not exist); andurel db migrate up; andurel doctor; andurel run; andurel verify.",
            "Pass --harness codex|claude|pi|opencode|crush (comma-separated or repeated) to install the bundled agent skill during creation. Without it the skill is not installed and the next steps print an explicit install example."
          ],
          "when_to_use": [
            "Create a new application directory from the current scaffold.",
            "Creation is offline: it installs no dependencies and needs no database."
          ],
          "when_not_to_use": [
            "Do not run inside an existing Andurel project."
          ],
          "next": [
            "cd \u003cproject\u003e",
            "andurel tool sync",
            "pnpm install (or bun/npm install to match --ui)",
            "cp .env.example .env",
            "andurel db create (only if the database does not exist)",
            "andurel db migrate up",
            "andurel doctor",
            "andurel run",
            "andurel verify"
          ],
          "examples": [
            "andurel new myapp",
            "andurel new myapp --ui vue/pnpm",
            "andurel new myapp --harness claude",
            "andurel new myapp --dry-run --json"
          ],
          "mutating": true,
          "supports_dry_run": true,
          "supports_json": true,
          "supports_jq": true,
          "supports_ids_only": false,
          "supports_count": false
        }
      },
