          {
            "name": "payloads",
            "path": "andurel sync payloads",
            "short": "Write TypeScript payload types for Inertia",
            "category": "sync",
            "meta": {
              "group": "sync",
              "summary": "Write TypeScript payload types for Inertia",
              "details": [
                "Scans handlers for inertia.FromStruct props (page props) and named structs decoded with anduin.DecodeJSON or anduin.DecodeForm (request payloads).",
                "Follows named struct fields into other packages in this Go module, so a handler prop may reference a type declared under internal/.",
                "Request payloads must be named with a Payload suffix; otherwise the sync fails and asks for a rename. Page props keep their struct name.",
                "Rejects domains/ types, unexported or generic structs, and fields with no TypeScript mapping; define a handler-owned payload instead.",
                "Skips literal inertia.Props{...} maps because there is no static struct to read, and omits fields tagged json:\"-\".",
                "Resolves FromStruct arguments passed as named composite literals, typed variables, function parameters, and closure parameters.",
                "Without --strict, an unresolved FromStruct argument is reported with its file:line and the hint to pass a named composite literal or a typed variable.",
                "--strict fails the command after writing resources/js/types/payloads.ts and lists every unresolved file:line; structured output keeps the same report as error data.",
                "Writes resources/js/types/payloads.ts."
              ],
              "when_to_use": [
                "After changing handler page props or request payload structs.",
                "Use --strict in CI to reject FromStruct arguments the scanner cannot resolve."
              ],
              "when_not_to_use": [
                "Use andurel inspect handlers to list handler files."
              ],
              "prerequisites": [
                "Andurel project root",
                "Inertia adapter in andurel.toml"
              ],
              "examples": [
                "andurel sync payloads --json",
                "andurel sync payloads --strict"
              ],
              "mutating": true,
              "requires_project": true,
              "supports_dry_run": false,
              "supports_json": true,
              "supports_jq": true,
              "supports_ids_only": false,
              "supports_count": false,
              "skip_dry_run_check": true
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "queries",
