          {
            "name": "routes",
            "path": "andurel sync routes",
            "short": "Write TypeScript route helpers for Inertia",
            "long": "Generate framework-neutral TypeScript route helpers for Inertia frontends.\n\nThe command reads routes/*.go as the source of truth and writes\nresources/js/routes.ts for Vue, React, or Svelte Inertia frontends. A route\nopts in with routing.TypeScriptRoute() (routing.InertiaRoute() is a deprecated\nalias), so JSON endpoints and asset URLs can get typed helpers too.\n\nA full-URL helper throws until origins are configured: browser entries call\nconfigureRouteHosts at boot and SSR entries wrap each render in\nwithRouteHosts. Use routes.\u003cname\u003e.path() for a relative URL.",
            "usage": "andurel sync routes",
            "examples": "andurel sync routes\n  andurel sync routes --json",
            "inherited_flags": [
              {
                "name": "agent",
                "usage": "Emit structured output optimized for agents",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "count",
                "usage": "Emit one raw resource count when supported",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "ids-only",
                "usage": "Emit one resource identifier per line when supported",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "jq",
                "usage": "Select a field path (for example .routes[0].name) from command data and emit JSON directly",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "name": "json",
                "usage": "Emit JSON output",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "md",
                "usage": "Emit Markdown output",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "quiet",
                "usage": "Suppress non-essential human output",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              },
              {
                "name": "verbose",
                "usage": "Emit verbose output",
                "default": "false",
                "type": "bool"
              }
            ],
            "agent_notes": "After adding or changing routes in routes/. After binding a route to a named host with routing.Host(...) so helpers embed the host and return full URLs.",
            "category": "sync",
            "meta": {
              "group": "sync",
              "summary": "Write TypeScript route helpers for Inertia",
              "details": [
                "Scans routes/*.go and writes resources/js/routes.ts for routes marked routing.TypeScriptRoute() (routing.InertiaRoute() is a deprecated alias).",
                "JSON endpoints and asset URLs can opt in, not only Inertia page routes.",
                "Full-URL helpers throw until configureRouteHosts (browser boot) or withRouteHosts (per SSR render) supplies origins; use routes.\u003cname\u003e.path() for relative URLs."
              ],
              "when_to_use": [
                "After adding or changing routes in routes/.",
                "After binding a route to a named host with routing.Host(...) so helpers embed the host and return full URLs."
              ],
              "when_not_to_use": [
                "Do not confuse with andurel inspect routes, which only lists the manifest."
              ],
              "prerequisites": [
                "Andurel project root",
                "Inertia adapter in andurel.toml"
              ],
              "next": [
                "andurel sync payloads"
              ],
              "examples": [
